ta-label pi-secondary-font\">Written by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"illustration\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Illustrated by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"colors\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Colors by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Miquel_Muerto\" title=\"Miquel Muerto\">Miquel Muerto</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"letters\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Lettered by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/AndWorld_Design\" title=\"AndWorld Design\">AndWorld Design</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"release_date\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Release date</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">September 4, 2019</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<table class=\"pi-horizontal-group\">\n\t<caption class=\"pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-secondary-background pi-item-spacing\">Chronology</caption>\n\t\n\t<thead>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<th class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-label pi-secondary-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"next\">Next →</th>\n\t\t\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</thead>\n\t\n\t<tbody>\n\t<tr>\n\t\n\t\t<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"next\"><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_2\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 2\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #2</a></td>\n\t\n\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #1</b> is a horror comic from <a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a> that was published on September 4, 2019 by <a href=\"/wiki/Boom!_Studios\" title=\"Boom! Studios\">Boom! Studios</a>. It is the first issue in the <i><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(comic_series)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (comic series)\">Something Is Killing the Children</a></i> comic series, the first issue of the five-part <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Angel_of_Archer%27s_Peak_(comic_arc)\" title=\"The Angel of Archer&#39;s Peak (comic arc)\">The Angel of Archer's Peak</a></i> arc, and the first issue of the fifteen-part <i>Archer's Peak</i> saga.\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Synopsis\">Synopsis</span></h2>\n<blockquote><p>GLAAD Award-winning writer <a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a> (<i>Memetic</i>, <i>Batman: Detective Comics</i>) teams with artist <a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a> (<i>Briggs Land</i>) for an all-new limited series about staring into the abyss to find your worst fears staring back.\n</p><p>When the children of Archer's Peak begin to go missing, everything seems hopeless. Most children never return, but the ones that do have terrible stories—impossible stories of terrifying creatures that live in the shadows.\n</p><p>Their only hope of finding and eliminating the threat is the arrival of a mysterious stranger, one who believes the children and claims to see what they can see.\n</p><p>\nHer name is <a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a>. She kills monsters. That is all she does, and she bears the cost because it MUST be done.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></p></blockquote>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Plot\">Plot</span></h2>\n<p>At a sleepover, a group of preteen boys play Truth or Dare. <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a> describes a monster he supposedly saw coming through the forest while he was home alone, to the disbelief of his friends. He then challenges <a href=\"/wiki/Noah\" title=\"Noah\">Noah</a> to go look under the bridge. Following, James is in the police station, the sole survivor of his group of friends. He tells the police that the monster he'd described had come and killed them all, but he doesn't understand, because he had made the story up. \n</p><p>Two weeks later, <a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a> comes out of the woods, bloodied, and meets with a little girl. She gets a call from <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a> to go to <a href=\"/wiki/Archer%27s_Peak\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak\">Archer's Peak</a>, which will take her sixteen hours. \n</p><p>At Archer's Peak, James is confronted at a memorial for several lost students by <a href=\"/wiki/Dan_Brisby\" title=\"Dan Brisby\">Dan Brisby</a>, who accuses him of killing the children due to his homosexuality. Robbie shouts at him to \"shut the fuck up,\" which gets him sent to the Principal's office. <a href=\"/wiki/John_Collins\" title=\"John Collins\">John Collins</a>, however, simply tells him that he probably should have punched him, before revealing that the police think the children are being killed by a bear. He apologizes for breaking in front of him, but James lets him know that it makes him feel better, before returning to class. \n</p><p>Erica, holding <a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a>, gets off the bus at Archer's Peak; a woman next to her remarks about the missing children. Erica looks at a large wall of missing posters, and a police officer asks if she knows any of the children. She says \"You could say that,\" before leaving. James arrives home at his family's hotel room, where they've been staying to avoid the press. Erica then approaches him, asking him to be honest about the monster he saw, swearing that she will believe him. James explains that he'd seen his friends ripped apart, before seeing Tyler being stabbed by a <a href=\"/wiki/Oscuratype\" title=\"Oscuratype\">monster</a>. After seeing Erica respond to a phone call, James realizes that Erica is here to kill the monster, and asks if he can help.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Characters\">Characters</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Order_of_St._George\"><a href=\"/wiki/Order_of_St._George\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Order of St. George\">Order of St. George</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span id=\"Archer.27s_Peak\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Archer's_Peak\"><a href=\"/wiki/Archer%27s_Peak\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak\">Archer's Peak</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Dan_Brisby\" title=\"Dan Brisby\">Dan Brisby</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Joe_Cavanaugh\" title=\"Joe Cavanaugh\">Sheriff Joe Cavanaugh</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/John_Collins\" title=\"John Collins\">Principal John Collins</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"James&#39;s Father (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSmFtZXMlMjdzX0ZhdGhlcj9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">James's Father</span> <small>(voicemail)</small></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Karl\" title=\"Karl\">Karl</a> †</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tyler_Monitz\" title=\"Tyler Monitz\">Tyler Monitz</a> †</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Noah\" title=\"Noah\">Noah</a> †</li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/John_Richards\" title=\"John Richards\">Officer John Richards</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Robbie\" title=\"Robbie\">Robbie</a> †</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Monsters\">Monsters</span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Oscuratype\" title=\"Oscuratype\">Oscuratype</a>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype mother (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfbW90aGVyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Archer's Peak Oscuratype mother</span></li></ul></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"5c08f66c1029c80ee490ff142c186064\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:187px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_1_Cover-jpg\" style=\"position: relative; height:185px; width:121px;\"><a class=\"image lightbox\" href=\"/wiki/File:Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_1_Cover.jpg\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 1 Cover.jpg (1.6 MB)\" style=\"height:185px; width:121px;\"><noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/e/e8/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_1_Cover.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/121?cb=20230225202450\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 1 Cover.jpg (1.6 MB)\" class=\"thumbimage\" alt=\"Something Is Killing the Children #1 cover by Werther Dell&#039;Edera\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Something Is Killing the Children 1 Co